    description: "Concept audit 2026-10-21/22 (pinned dev e9215548f6; write-up ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/concept_audit_10212026/concept-audit-vocabulary-since-0923_10222026.md). F3, verified by reading receiver_blind_magnets.py:247-251 (src_owner = owner_of(src.name) is None for a type anchor named 'P', so the same-class exemption never applies) + agent probe: Java/C# class P { static int Parse(String s); static int X = Parse(\"1\"); } -> the class-anchored edge to P.Parse is demoted by finalize.py:409 to java:external:0-0:Parse:unresolved; the same call from a method is kept. Fix: an anchor of kind type owns itself (owner = its own name). Repro through the production CLI first."  # 4d32
