- op: discuss  # 4e5a
  at: '2026-10-25T20:08:21Z'  # 4e5a
  by: agent  # 4e5a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4e5a
  clock: 2  # 4e5a
  nonce: 4e5a  # 4e5a
  message: "Premise re-check 2026-10-25 on dev 16534a75f7 (production-CLI repros on tiny fixtures unless marked code read). CURRENT. Java `class P { static int Parse(String s); static int compute(String s); static int X = Parse(\"1\"); static int Y = compute(\"1\"); static int fromMethod(){ return Parse(\"2\"); } }` publishes P:class -> java:external:0-0:Parse:unresolved (ambiguous, 0.5) while fromMethod -> P.Parse is kept at 0.85; analyze_java binds P -> P.Parse at 0.85 before finalize. C# and Kotlin behave the same; a nested Outer.Inner anchoring Close(\"1\") is demoted too. Refs: receiver_blind_magnets.py:247-251 accurate; demotion call finalize.py:410 (function :391); _harmful_magnet_reason :299-321; _STDLIB_INTERFACE_METHODS :261-285. Scope is narrower than the title: the detector misflags EVERY class-anchored own-method call (compute too), but finalize demotes only for the ~25 stdlib-interface names (Parse, Close, Read, Write, String, Error, Len, Value...). Fix precision: for a type-like src kind the owner is the anchor's full generic-stripped name, NOT owner_of(name) -- owner_of('Outer.Inner') is 'Outer' while owner_of('Outer.Inner.Close') is 'Outer.Inner'; per the ADR-0023 contract (WI-fazup) a consumer reads the src kind. The regression test must include the nested case. Unchecked side gap: Python `class C: def Read(s): ...; x = Read(\"1\")` gives C:class -> python:external:0-0:Read:external_symbol. P2 kept."  # 4e5a
