- op: discuss  # de0c
  at: '2026-10-26T09:10:48Z'  # de0c
  by: agent  # de0c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # de0c
  clock: 4  # de0c
  nonce: de0c  # de0c
  message: "DONE in PR #1874 (merged, dev 1b50a90482). Root cause: the same-owner exemption read the caller's owner as owner_of(name), and a class-kind anchor is its own owner (owner_of('P') is None, owner_of('Outer.Inner') is 'Outer'). Fix: _caller_owner returns the generic-stripped full name for a src whose kind is in type_like_kind_names() (read off the node, per the ADR-0023 kind contract), owner_of otherwise.\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, the filed repro re-run on merged dev: Java `class Outer { static int Parse(String s); static int compute(String s); static int X = Parse(\"1\"); static int Y = compute(\"1\"); static int fromMethod(){ return Parse(\"2\"); } static class Inner { static int Close(String s); static int Z = Close(\"1\"); } }` -> Outer -> Outer.Parse 0.85 (was java:external:0-0:Parse:unresolved), Outer.Inner -> Outer.Inner.Close 0.85 (the nested case), fromMethod unchanged. Production-path tests for java, csharp and kotlin (test_magnet_demotion_keeps_typed_binds.py); unit controls that a class anchor calling ANOTHER class's method, and an outer anchor calling a nested class's method, are still flagged.\nMEASURED: jenkins and spring-petclinic 0 type-anchor demotions (camelCase methods rarely hit the PascalCase list); C# effect unmeasured (no C#-heavy repo on hand). The Python side gap in the premise note is NOT this defect: `class C: def Read(s): ...; x = Read(\"1\")` publishes C -> python:external:0-0:Read:external_symbol for compute too, i.e. the python analyzer does not bind a class-body bare call to a class-scope function at all -- filed separately."  # de0c
